# models/Issue.js — add two fields

The classifier now runs server-side. Record what it said, separately from
what the client submitted, so an admin can spot misrouted issues.

Add inside the schema, next to `aiTagged` / `aiConf`:

```js
  aiTagged: { type: Boolean, default: false },
  aiConf:   { type: Number },                  // percentage 0-100

  // What the server-side classifier suggested. Kept separate from
  // `category` because the client picks the final value from a dropdown.
  // When these disagree, the issue is a reroute candidate.
  aiSuggestedCategory: { type: String },
```

Nothing else in the model changes. `aiSuggestedCategory` is internal — the
citizen serializer never reads it, and `toOfficerView` / `toAdminView` can
surface it for the reroute UI.